<?php

namespace App\Services\Agreements;

use InvalidArgumentException;

/** Negotiated Avery terms only; no entitlement, provider, invoice or payment mutation. */
class AveryAgreementTerms
{
    public const POLICY_VERSION = 'avery-service-exit-2026-10-18-v1';

    public const GOVERNING_STATE = 'South Carolina';

    public const VENUE_COUNTY = 'Pickens';

    public function apply(array $payload, ?string $state = null, ?string $county = null): array
    {
        if (($payload['termination']['policy_version'] ?? null) === self::POLICY_VERSION) {
            return $payload;
        }

        $state ??= self::GOVERNING_STATE;
        $county ??= self::VENUE_COUNTY;
        if (trim($state) === '' || trim($county) === '') {
            throw new InvalidArgumentException('Confirm Evergrove governing state and court county before issuing Avery terms.');
        }

        $sections = [
            'Launch scope and capacity' => 'The initial launch covers one Avery Knifeworks business workspace and up to five named users with individual role-based access. Before implementation, the parties will confirm a written launch checklist identifying the approved catalog and handle variants, supported inventory/material-lot, production, order, shipping and customer-care workflows, import files, contact/storage/channel limits, and provider readiness. The five-user commitment must be supported by the confirmed production plan before activation. A demonstration does not activate unreleased features or unapproved integrations. If the proposed scope cannot be delivered, the parties must agree a revised scope or cancel with the refund treatment below; payment does not waive launch requirements.',
            'Included routine support and changes' => 'While service is active and paid, the monthly price includes up to two consolidated routine update requests per calendar month, with one reasonable revision round for each request. Each request covers one coherent update to existing approved content or standard configuration using accurate client-supplied materials. Unused requests and revision rounds do not roll over. Evergrove targets acknowledgment of complete requests within three business days, excluding weekends and public holidays observed by its office. This is an acknowledgment target, not a completion or uptime guarantee. Defect reports and security reports do not consume the routine-update allowance. New features, custom code, redesigns, bulk migrations, additional integrations and other work outside the written launch scope require a separate written quote and approval before work or charges begin; the existing $50/hour rate applies unless a different fixed quote is approved.',
            'Month-to-month service and cancellation' => 'Service continues month to month at $299 per business unless cancelled. Either party may give written cancellation notice before the next renewal; ordinary cancellation takes effect at the end of the current paid service period. There is no multi-month minimum or early-termination penalty. Evergrove will acknowledge the notice and confirm the effective date, final billing and export deadline in writing. Cancellation stops future subscription renewals and automatic usage reloads after the effective date. The client may request an earlier stop to new chargeable marketing or AI activity. No automatic card charge is authorized without a separate valid payment-provider authorization. Earned setup fees, authorized usage and separately approved third-party or custom-work charges incurred before the applicable cutoff remain payable.',
            'Final usage billing and prepaid-credit refunds' => 'Cancellation does not erase charges for email, SMS/MMS, AI or other services actually used or irrevocably committed with the client’s authorization before the agreed stop time. Delayed provider reporting may produce a closing adjustment at the Everbranch unit or model rates approved when the activity occurred. Evergrove will apply available purchased credit to authorized unpaid charges first and issue a separate itemized invoice for any remaining amount, due 15 calendar days after delivery. Usage already deducted from prepaid credit is not billed again. This settlement rule does not authorize overdrafts, higher spending limits, retroactive rate changes, new provider activity or automatic card collection. No charge applies merely because credit was purchased or a future feature was selected.',
            'Closing statement and unused balance' => 'Evergrove will provide an initial closing statement within 15 business days after termination, showing usage dates, service, quantity, applicable rate or model calculation, deductions, paid credit purchases, documented pending commitments, refunds and any unpaid balance. Unused purchased credit is refundable after settling authorized usage and unpaid charges; promotional, bonus or gifted credit has no cash-refund value. Undisputed refundable amounts will be returned to the original payment method, or an agreed alternative if unavailable, within 30 calendar days after termination. Only a reasonable, itemized reserve for identifiable pending authorized charges or a specific good-faith dispute may be held; unrelated undisputed credit is refunded on time. Provider true-ups and release of reserves should be completed within 60 calendar days after termination. If a documented provider dispute prevents that deadline, Evergrove will explain the amount and reason in writing and give updates at least every 30 days until resolved. The client may dispute an item promptly with supporting details; undisputed invoice amounts remain due, and this process does not waive mandatory legal rights.',
            'Setup fees, partial months and service remedies' => 'The $499 setup fee is earned as the agreed setup work is completed. If the engagement ends before setup is completed, Evergrove will provide a reasonable accounting of completed work and approved nonrecoverable commitments and refund the unearned balance; there is no additional cancellation penalty. Ordinary client cancellation leaves service available through the paid month and does not create a partial-month subscription refund. If Evergrove ends service early without client breach, or an uncured material Evergrove breach justifies early termination, prepaid subscription fees for the unused period will be refunded proportionately. The parties will first try reasonable correction or reperformance of an agreed service failure. The initial invoice remains $798 before applicable tax, with no usage fees or prepaid-credit purchase, and the first month is not charged twice.',
            'Client data, website identity and domains' => 'Avery retains its business name, trademarks, branding, original content, photographs, product and handle information, customer and order records, inventory and material-lot data, knife passport and care/service history, and lawfully held communication-consent and opt-out records. A custom domain registered for Avery is to be registered in Avery’s name where the registrar permits, with Avery designated for ownership and recovery access. Evergrove’s administrative management does not transfer domain ownership. Domain registration, renewal and third-party licensing costs require the agreed scope or separate approval. Avery keeps its client-specific website identity and may reuse its own content and general visual design direction with another provider, subject to third-party asset licenses.',
            'Included export and transition package' => 'An authorized Avery representative may request one standard transition package during the notice period or within 30 calendar days after the effective termination date. Evergrove will provide reasonably available Avery-owned site copy, original photographs/files, product and handle information, design direction and exportable customer, order, inquiry, inventory/material-lot, production, shipping, knife-passport, service-history and communication-permission records then held in the agreed service. Data will use a reasonably available common format such as CSV, XLSX or JSON, with assets in their available original formats. The included export has no separate exit fee. Delivery is targeted within 10 business days after a complete, verified request; a timely request remains eligible if delivery extends beyond the 30-day window. Evergrove will explain any unavailable fields or technical limitation. Basic export is not withheld solely because of a good-faith billing dispute; undisputed fees remain payable. Additional data cleanup, imports, rebuilding or migration labor requires a separate approved quote.',
            'Moving to another provider and platform rights' => 'The package supports recreating a comparable Avery site or business workflow on Wix or another service; re-entry, rebuilding and destination-provider fees may be necessary. It is not a promise of a working clone, a one-click transfer or equivalent features elsewhere. Evergrove retains Everbranch source code, reusable themes and components, editor, hosted forms/data services, automations, integrations, version history software, AI tools and other licensed platform capabilities. These are not transferred as client-owned software or kept active after termination. Exportable Avery business records remain Avery’s even when generated through those tools. Ownership or licensing of separately commissioned custom code must be stated in its own signed work order; payment alone does not transfer the platform or third-party intellectual property.',
            'Connected accounts and dedicated numbers' => 'Avery retains ownership/control of accounts it establishes directly with a registrar, payment processor or other provider. Evergrove will reasonably assist with transferring Avery-controlled administrative access and removing its own access after an authorized handoff. A separately approved dedicated Avery telephone number may be ported or transferred where the carrier/provider permits, after required verification and payment of approved provider charges. Shared platform numbers, temporary demonstration senders, messaging registrations and platform-owned credentials are not automatically transferable. External provider processing, eligibility and timing are outside Evergrove’s control; any continuing account or renewal charges must be identified. Provider integrations, scheduled sends, hosted forms, editing, support, automations and live AI/voice access stop at termination except a separately agreed transition service. The export window provides a way to obtain records, not an additional month of active software, hosting or sending.',
            'Data use, confidentiality and security' => 'Each party will protect the other’s nonpublic business information and use it only for the agreed service, support, billing, security, legal obligations and authorized integrations. Exceptions cover information already lawfully known, independently developed, lawfully received without restriction or public without breach. Necessary service providers may receive only information needed for their approved role under appropriate confidentiality and data-protection terms; legally required disclosures are permitted with notice where lawful. Evergrove will not sell Avery’s data, share it for unrelated third-party marketing or use it to train shared AI models without separate written permission. Evergrove will use reasonable safeguards appropriate to the agreed data, including encrypted transport, access controls, credential protection, backups and incident response, and notify Avery without undue delay after confirming unauthorized access or disclosure affecting its information, subject to applicable law. Avery controls its users and permissions and supplies lawful, accurate data; payment-card security codes and unnecessary sensitive personal information must not be uploaded to general workspace fields.',
            'Retention, deletion and surviving records' => 'Operational records remain eligible for export through the 30-day post-termination window and completion of a timely export request. After that point, Evergrove will remove active operational copies within 30 calendar days unless a longer period is required by law or separately agreed in writing. Residual backup copies will expire through the normal backup cycle within a further 90 calendar days and will not be used for ordinary business processing; if restored for recovery, applicable deletion restrictions will be reapplied. Signed agreements, billing, payment, security, legal-hold and audit records may be retained only as needed for applicable obligations or legitimate claim records, with restricted access. Third-party accounts the client retains are subject to their own retention rules. Confidentiality, ownership, unpaid authorized charges, refunds, dispute provisions and rights intended to survive remain in effect after termination.',
            'Suspension, breach and early termination' => 'For a material breach, including nonpayment of an undisputed amount, the other party may give written notice identifying the issue and allow 10 business days to cure before terminating affected service. A genuine billing dispute is handled through the closing-statement process while undisputed amounts are paid. Evergrove may immediately limit or suspend affected functionality where reasonably necessary to address a serious security threat, unlawful use, significant abuse or a legal requirement; it will give prompt notice and an explanation where lawful, keep the response proportionate, and restore service when the reason is resolved. Persistent uncured breach may lead to termination on a written effective date. Suspension is not an early-termination penalty and does not authorize new chargeable activity. Authorized fees incurred before the stop remain due; applicable export, refund and legal-retention obligations continue.',
            'AI assistance and approval controls' => 'AI output may be incomplete or inaccurate and requires appropriate human review, particularly for product claims, warranty promises, prices, customer communications, manufacturing, tax and fulfillment decisions. Avery supplies and maintains the permissions and opt-outs required for its communications. The demo does not itself authorize messages, payments, publication or shipping purchases; production actions require the approved scope, provider readiness, user permissions and spending authorization. Future memory, telephone voice, recordings and customer-facing AI require their separate release, agreed data/retention and consent settings, approved rate schedule and readiness before activation. Nothing here promises unreleased capabilities or unlimited usage.',
            'Liability allocation' => 'To the extent permitted by applicable law, neither party is liable to the other for indirect or consequential losses, including lost profits or business opportunities arising from this agreement. Each party’s aggregate liability arising from this agreement is limited to the greater of $1,000 or the setup and subscription fees paid or payable to Evergrove under this agreement during the 12 months before the event giving rise to the claim; taxes, postage, purchased unused credit and metered third-party usage are excluded from that fee calculation. These limits do not reduce authorized payment obligations, required refunds or return of client funds, and do not apply to fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence or liability that cannot lawfully be limited. No clause transfers Avery’s product-manufacturing, product-safety or warranty responsibilities to Evergrove. This allocation is subject to mandatory law and does not remove an expressly agreed service remedy.',
            'Notices, disputes and governing law' => 'Contract, cancellation and billing notices go to john@evergrovesoftware.com for Evergrove and to the client notice email supplied by Avery’s authorized signer or updated in writing. A notice is effective when received; delivery failures must be corrected, and Evergrove will acknowledge cancellation and billing-dispute notices. The parties will first seek a good-faith business resolution for 30 calendar days after written dispute notice. This does not bar a competent small-claims court, urgent injunctive relief or action needed to preserve a legal deadline. The laws of '.$state.', without its conflict-of-law rules, govern this agreement except where mandatory law requires otherwise. Subject to mandatory jurisdiction rules, court proceedings will be brought in the state courts serving '.$county.' County, '.$state.', or the federal court with jurisdiction there. Changes to scope, rates or these terms require a written amendment accepted by authorized representatives; an invoice, website change or feature selection alone does not amend the agreement.',
        ];

        $existing = collect($payload['scope']['sections'])->keyBy('title')->all();
        $existing['First invoice and subsequent months']['body'] .= ' Service month 1 starts when the approved production workspace is activated, or on another start date expressly agreed in writing; opening the demonstration or making the initial payment alone does not start a second monthly charge. The first renewal follows that covered month.';
        foreach ($sections as $title => $body) {
            $existing[$title] = ['title' => $title, 'body' => $body];
        }
        if (trim((string) ($payload['scope']['additional_scope'] ?? '')) !== '') {
            $existing['Additional agreed Avery scope'] = ['title' => 'Additional agreed Avery scope', 'body' => $payload['scope']['additional_scope']];
        }
        unset($existing['Client data and ownership']);
        $payload['scope']['sections'] = array_values($existing);
        $payload['content']['scope_sections'] = $payload['scope']['sections'];
        $payload['scope']['support_policy'] = ['requests_per_calendar_month' => 2, 'revision_rounds_per_request' => 1, 'acknowledgment_business_days' => 3, 'rollover' => false, 'defect_reports_consume_allowance' => false];
        $payload['scope']['capacity_commitment'] = ['business_workspaces' => 1, 'named_users' => 5, 'activation_requires_verified_capacity' => true];
        $payload['scope']['implementation_phases'] = [
            ['phase' => '1', 'title' => 'Confirm scope and prepare the private workspace', 'deliverables' => ['Confirm supported modules, five-user capacity, limits, import files, account ownership and provider readiness in a written launch checklist.', 'Configure the approved initial catalog, variants and supported operations privately; review import results with Avery.']],
            ['phase' => '2', 'title' => 'Review, approve and hand off', 'deliverables' => ['Review desktop/mobile storefront, authorized users and the supported order, inventory, shipping and care workflows against the checklist; correct agreed launch-blocking issues.', 'Record launch approval, the service start and first renewal dates; confirm the initial invoice already includes month 1. Activate only after existing agreement, payment, capacity and provider gates pass.']],
            ['phase' => '3', 'title' => 'Maintain the agreed service', 'deliverables' => ['Provide routine support within the approved monthly allowance and maintain approved platform service.', 'Keep new custom work, future features and additional integrations subject to separate written approval and readiness; retain itemized usage and spending controls.']],
        ];
        $payload['content']['implementation_phases'] = $payload['scope']['implementation_phases'];
        $payload['content']['ownership']['client'] = $sections['Client data, website identity and domains'];
        $payload['content']['ownership']['provider'] = 'Evergrove retains the platform, source code, reusable components and licensed capabilities. Avery’s exportable business records and supplied assets remain Avery’s; custom-work rights and third-party licenses follow their separate written terms.';
        $payload['content']['client_responsibilities'] = 'Avery supplies accurate, rights-cleared content, timely approvals and authorized users; verifies its catalog, imports, product safety, manufacturing, stock, fulfillment, taxes and guarantee promises; and maintains lawful marketing consent and opt-outs. Client delays or missing information may move the launch schedule.';
        $payload['content']['platform_availability'] = 'Reasonable maintenance, provider outages and security response may affect service. No sales result, uninterrupted uptime, carrier approval, future feature or release date is guaranteed. The support acknowledgment target is not a completion deadline.';
        $payload['termination'] = [...$payload['termination'], 'policy_version' => self::POLICY_VERSION,
            'notice' => 'Written notice before the next monthly renewal; ordinary cancellation takes effect at the end of the current paid service period.',
            'terms' => [
                'Avery retains its business records, supplied assets, website identity and client-owned domains. Everbranch software and licensed features remain Evergrove’s.',
                'New subscription renewals, automatic reloads, hosted operations and provider activity stop at the agreed cutoff, except a separately agreed transition service.',
                'Previously authorized usage actually incurred or irrevocably committed remains payable at the approved rates. Apply available purchased credit first; invoice only the unpaid remainder, due 15 calendar days after delivery. Already deducted usage is not billed again.',
                'Provide an initial closing statement within 15 business days. Refund undisputed unused purchased credit after settlement within 30 calendar days; promotional credit has no cash value. Documented reserves and provider true-ups follow the Closing statement and unused balance section.',
                'One standard export package is included at no exit fee, requested during notice or within 30 days after termination, with a 10-business-day delivery target after a complete verified request. A timely request remains eligible through completion.',
                'The export window does not extend active software service. Record deletion, backup expiry and restricted legal/audit retention follow the Retention, deletion and surviving records section.',
            ],
            'settlement' => ['authorized_incurred_usage_remains_payable' => true, 'already_deducted_usage_billed_again' => false, 'purchased_credit_refundable' => true, 'promotional_credit_cash_refundable' => false, 'invoice_due_calendar_days' => 15, 'initial_statement_business_days' => 15, 'undisputed_refund_calendar_days' => 30, 'provider_true_up_target_calendar_days' => 60, 'automatic_card_collection_authorized' => false],
            'export' => ['request_during_notice' => true, 'request_after_termination_days' => 30, 'included_standard_packages' => 1, 'delivery_target_business_days' => 10, 'basic_exit_fee_cents' => 0, 'format' => 'reasonably available CSV, XLSX or JSON and original available asset formats'],
        ];

        return $payload;
    }
}
